meta {
  name: Fetch VPAs by Phone
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/vpas/phone/{{vendorLookupIdentifier}}/fetch
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{vahnAdminToken}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  `VPAResource.fetchVPA`, roles VAHN_ADMIN and TORG_ADMIN. Looks the phone number up through
  Surepass and saves the returned VPAs (writes staging data, bills one Surepass call); the response
  is a list of VPA entities.

  Known quirk (pre-existing, not ENG-1309): the resource returns the raw `VPA` entities, and each
  `driver` nests its `vpas` back to the VPA again, so on staging the body is ~1.1 MB of
  driver/vpa nesting about 250 levels deep. Bruno cannot parse it (`res.body` is a string), so
  this request only asserts the HTTP status. Use a phone with no linked driver for a small body.

  ENG-1309: a Surepass outage now gives body `statusCode: 503` (was 400). The HTTP status stays 200
  because ApiResponseFilter rewrites it. Not reproducible on staging.
}
